          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Avoid taking tricks containing high-value cards. The first player to accumulate 2,000 points loses the entire session.',
          gameplay: "1. Must follow suit. If unable, must play a trump (Jack) if held.\n2. Highest Jack wins; if no Jack, highest card of led suit wins.\n3. **Kontra/Re**: Before playing the first card, players can 'double' the value of the round points.",
          keyRules: [
            'Ace: 11 points',
            'Ten: 10 points',
            'King: 4 points',
            'Queen: 3 points',
            'Jack (Trump): 2 points',
            '7, 8, 9: 0 points',
            'Jacks are permanent trumps. Ranking: Clubs (High) > Spades > Hearts > Diamonds (Low).',
            'Must follow suit; if unable, must play a trump Jack if held',
            'Only the player who takes the MOST points in a round receives those points as penalty',
            'Durchmarsch (winning all 8 tricks): Scorer gets 0, others take 120-point penalty',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Dump your Aces and Tens on tricks that OTHER players win. The goal is to stay 'under' the point threshold of the biggest loser of the round.",
          intermediate: "Duck Tricks: Even if you could win a trick, sometimes it's better to play a low 7 or 8 to ensure you aren't forced to lead the next trick (which is always dangerous).",
          advanced: 'The Durchmarsch Gambit: If you hold 3+ Jacks and several Aces, you might try to win every single trick. This is high risk; if you miss even one trick, you will likely end up with the most points and take the penalty.',
          tips: [
            "Jacks are only 2 points but they 'pull' other cards. Use them to force opponents to play their Aces.",
            "The 'Kalter Schlag' (surprise loss) usually happens in the 6th or 7th trick when a player is 'squeezed' into winning a 20+ point trick.",
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
